## Backend — Slice 2 (REST endpoint + cache wiring)

### Routes (`server/routes/codeAuthorship.ts`, NEW, ~120 lines)

```
GET  /api/work-items/:workItemId/code-authorship?refresh=false
       Returns WorkItemAuthorship. Reads from cache when fresh
       (computed_at within last 5 min AND branch_head_sha matches
       current). Otherwise computes, writes cache, returns.

GET  /api/work-items/:workItemId/code-authorship/files/:filePath/blame
       Returns line-by-line blame for a single file with
       per-line classification — for the drill-down diff viewer
       (slice 3).
```

Both endpoints derive `workspaceDir` + branch info from the work item's existing source-workspace metadata (the same path the artifact diff viewer already walks).

### Cache invalidation hook

In `server/agentGit/session.ts` (or wherever `agent_branch_commits` rows are inserted), call `invalidateAuthorshipCache(workItemId)` right after the INSERT. One-line change. Human-commit invalidation is left as a TODO documented in code; for V1 the 5-minute TTL is the safety net.

